<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Long Biên</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Long Biên was an ancient city in the Red River delta near present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a>, the administrative seat of Chinese-ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiaozhi">Jiaozhi</a> under the Han and later dynasties. During the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ly-nam-de">Lý Bí</a>, who proclaimed himself Lý Nam Đế in 544, it served as his base, and he built the Khai Quốc pagoda nearby. Its name survives in a district of Hanoi.</p></div>
